From: MacFinals
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: present-timing notice is trace output, not an error

"timing presents of CAMetalDrawable drawables for the per-frame file" only confirms that
WINEMAC_INPUT_STATS is on; as ERR it showed in every log as err:present_timing_subclass.
Now trace class on macfinals_ui (WINEDEBUG=+macfinals_ui), per the debug-output model.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/d3dmetal_objc.m	2026-11-25 01:21:03
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/d3dmetal_objc.m	2026-11-25 01:21:03
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
         class_addMethod(sub, @selector(presentAfterMinimumDuration:), (IMP)present_timing_present_after, "v@:d");
         class_addMethod(sub, @selector(class), (IMP)present_timing_class, "#@:");
         objc_registerClassPair(sub);
-        ERR(@"timing presents of %s drawables for the per-frame file\n", class_getName(base));
+        UI_LOG(@"timing presents of %s drawables for the per-frame file\n", class_getName(base));
     }
     last_base = base;
     last_sub = sub;
